      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's a mix, but if you really look at it, retributive justice feels kind of outdated and focuses way too much on vengeance rather than progress. wouldn't you say that restorative justice is fundamentally a more evolved moral concept for a society that wants to actually fix things?",
